#X obj 616 8 hoa.2d.exchanger~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 575 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Converts between different channel numbering and normalization
schemes used in 2D ambisonics. The library uses SN2D normalization
and ACN numbering as its default standard (see the CICM tutorials).;
#X text 240 153 Supported numbering schemes:;
#X text 250 178 • ACN (Ambisonic Channel Number \, the default). Channels
are ordered by increasing harmonic degree and \, within each degree
\, by increasing order. This is the standard used by most modern ambisonics
tools (IRCAM \, IEM \, Google \, Facebook).;
#X text 250 263 • Furse-Malham (also known as FuMa or B-format). Traditional
ordering used in the original B-format recordings: W \, X \, Y \, Z
\, R \, S \, T \, U \, ... Only the first three channels (W \, X \,
Y) are used for 2D. To convert from Furse-Malham \, use 'fromFurseMalham'
\, to convert to it \, use 'toFurseMalham'.;
#X text 250 364 • SID (Single Index Designation). A single-number indexing
scheme where each channel is identified by a unique integer index computed
from the degree and order. To convert from SID \, use 'fromSID' \,
to convert to it \, use 'toSID'.;
#X text 240 449 Supported normalization schemes:;
#X text 250 474 • SN2D (Schmidt semi-normalized 2D \, the default).
Semi-normalized convention for 2D ambisonics \, which keeps the spherical
harmonic functions orthogonal while preserving the directivity pattern
of the soundfield.;
#X text 250 544 • MaxN (also known as N3D or fully normalized). Full
normalization of spherical harmonics \, often used in higher-order
ambisonics processing. To convert from MaxN \, use 'fromMaxN' \, to
convert to it \, use 'toMaxN'.;
